    {
      "id": "chambers",
      "summary": "Chambers-wide AI deployment needs controls suited to shared systems and independent practices. The BSB guidance highlights procurement, data access and governance, including the risk of one barrister's client information becoming accessible to another. Chambers management is not the SRA COLP role. Governance priorities for chambers. Identify the actual duty-holder and relevant practice structure before applying any Handbook rule to a manager personally.",
      "priorities": [
        {
          "title": "Separate members\u2019 data",
          "text": "Test isolation between members' client information, particularly where members act for opposing parties.",
          "sourceUrl": "https://www.barstandardsboard.org.uk/static/5e1baa5c-614c-4105-afae9a9ccdf8d97b/c0d1ed62-fcad-4a68-8ab810de5fa9b116/Artificial-Intelligence-Guidance-May-2026.pdf"
        },
        {
          "title": "Provider settings",
          "text": "Set appropriate provider access, retention, deletion and shared-assistant settings.",
          "sourceUrl": "https://www.barstandardsboard.org.uk/static/5e1baa5c-614c-4105-afae9a9ccdf8d97b/c0d1ed62-fcad-4a68-8ab810de5fa9b116/Artificial-Intelligence-Guidance-May-2026.pdf"
        },
        {
          "title": "Shared procedures",
          "text": "Agree practical acceptable-use, training and incident procedures while preserving each barrister's professional responsibility.",
          "sourceUrl": "https://www.barstandardsboard.org.uk/static/5e1baa5c-614c-4105-afae9a9ccdf8d97b/c0d1ed62-fcad-4a68-8ab810de5fa9b116/Artificial-Intelligence-Guidance-May-2026.pdf"
        }
